### Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ Don't add custom styling to base components:
```tsx
// Wrong
<YStack padding="$5" space="$3">
<Button theme="active">
<Text fontSize="$6">
```

✅ Use default styling:
```tsx
// Correct
<YStack gap="$4" p="$4">
<Button>
<Text>
```

❌ Don't use React Native's ScrollView:
```tsx
// Wrong
import { ScrollView } from "react-native"
```

✅ Use Tamagui's ScrollView:
```tsx
// Correct
import { ScrollView } from "tamagui"
```

Refer to @.cursor/rules/ui-components-docs.mdc for component selection priority and styling guidelines.

## Header Visibility Rules

### Nested Navigation Headers
When using nested navigation (e.g., Tabs + Stack), follow these header visibility rules:

1. Root Layout (`app/_layout.tsx`):
```tsx
<Stack>
  <Stack.Screen name="(tabs)" options={{ headerShown: false }} />
  {/* Modal screens can show their headers */}
  <Stack.Screen
    name="account"
    options={{
      headerLeft: () => <CloseButton />,
      presentation: "modal",
      animation: "slide_from_bottom",
    }}
  />
</Stack>
```

2. Tab Layout (`app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx`):
```tsx
<Tabs
  screenOptions={{
    headerShown: false, // Hide tab navigator headers
  }}
>
  <Tabs.Screen name="(index)" options={{ title: "Home" }} />
  <Tabs.Screen name="portfolio" options={{ title: "Portfolio" }} />
</Tabs>
```

3. Stack Layout (e.g., `app/(tabs)/(index)/_layout.tsx`):
```tsx
<Stack>
  {/* Show headers only in the lowest level navigator */}
  <Stack.Screen name="index" options={{ title: "Home" }} />
  <Stack.Screen name="detail" options={{ title: "Detail" }} />
</Stack>
```

Key requirements:
- Hide headers in parent navigators (`headerShown: false`)
- Only show headers in the lowest level navigator
- Exception: Modal screens can show their headers with close buttons
- This creates a cleaner UI with only one visible header at a time 

## Navigation Path Rules

### Link Path Resolution
When creating navigation links using the `Link` component, the path format depends on the folder type:

1. Links from `(index)` folder:
```tsx
// ✅ Correct: Direct path without folder name
<Link href="/detail" />

// ❌ Incorrect: Including (index) in the path
<Link href="/(index)/detail" />
```

2. Links from normal folders (e.g., 'markets', 'settings'):
```tsx
// ✅ Correct: Include folder name in path
<Link href="/markets/detail" />

// ❌ Incorrect: Direct path without folder name
<Link href="/detail" />
```

This is because:
- The `(index)` folder is not included in the URL segment
- Normal folders (without parentheses) ARE included in the URL segment
- Always use absolute paths starting with "/"

### Examples

1. From Home Screen (`app/(tabs)/(index)/index.tsx`):
```tsx
// To home detail
<Link href="/detail" />

// To modals
<Link href="/login" />
<Link href="/signup" />
```

2. From Markets Screen (`app/(tabs)/markets/index.tsx`):
```tsx
// To markets detail
<Link href="/markets/detail" />

// To modals (same as from home)
<Link href="/login" />
<Link href="/signup" />
```